abstract:
This paper examines the behavior of a positive solution $u\in C^{1,α}(\BarΩ)$ of the $(p,q)$ Laplace equation with a singular term and zero Dirichlet boundary condition. Specifically, we consider the equation:  egin{equation*} -div(|
abla u|^{p-2}
abla u+ a(x) |
abla u|^{q-2}
abla u) &=  rac{g(x)}{u^δ}+h(x)f(u) \, &	ext{in} 	hinspace B_R(x_0), \quad u & =0 \ &	ext{on} \ \partial B_R(x_0). \end{equation*} We assume that $0<δ<1$, $1<p\leq q<\infty$, and $f$ is a $C^1(\mathbb{R})$ nondecreasing function. Our analysis uses the moving plane method to investigate the symmetry and monotonicity properties of $u$. Additionally, we establish a strong comparison principle for solutions of the $(p,q)$ Laplace equation with radial symmetry under the assumptions that $1<p\leq q\leq 2$ and $f\equiv1$.
